<Layout title="Team" description="Researchers and students of the HelioFísica y Clima Espacial USACH group.">

<section>
  <span class="section-title">Team</span>
  <h1>Our team</h1>
  <p class="lead">Researchers, master's and undergraduate students of the Heliophysics and Space Weather group at USACH.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="section-title">Principal Investigators</span>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Dr. Victor A. Pinto Abarzúa</h3>
      <p><strong>Assistant Professor</strong> · Department of Physics, USACH</p>
      <p>Ph.D. in Atmospheric and Oceanic Sciences (Space Physics), UCLA 2019. Postdoc at UNH (2020-2022). Researcher in radiation belts, ULF waves, space weather and machine learning.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:0.75rem">
        <a href="https://victorapinto.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Personal site</a> ·
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=nEqGWqoAAAAJ" target="_blank">Google Scholar</a> ·
        <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1210-167X" target="_blank">ORCID</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Prof. Marina Stepanova</h3>
      <p><strong>Professor</strong> · Department of Physics, USACH</p>
      <p>Ph.D. in Astrophysics, Skobeltsyn Institute, Moscow State University. Researcher in space plasmas, magnetospheric dynamics, turbulence, geomagnetic storms and substorms. At USACH since 1995. Head of the B.S. Astrophysics + Data Science degree program.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:0.75rem">
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Rb-PfE4AAAAJ" target="_blank">Google Scholar</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

